content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   This session continued work on `lobu apply`'s drift gate. The user's explicit requests, chronologically:
   - **"yes you need to test e2e and make sure it all looks ok and working proeprly"** — after I merged PR #2686 on unit-level evidence alone, demand real end-to-end verification.
   - **"why do you keep legacy instead of migrating all the legacy stuff into the new system. also you need to test"** — challenge the existence of a permanent "legacy" (unrecorded-baseline) code path, and test whatever conclusion I reach.
   - **"yes let's do those"** — proceed with the three follow-ups I had enumerated: (1) fix the prune-off block, (2) render before → after values in the plan, (3) drop/re-scope `--bootstrap`.
   - **"ok go do those"** — ship both PRs (gates, commit, push, PR, review, merge).

   Standing constraints from CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md still in force: never write to `~/Code/lobu` directly (worktrees only, via `make task-setup NAME=<slug>`); never `git stash`; never `git checkout` to undo a mutation (use `cp` from a backup); stage by explicit path with `git add -- <paths>`, never `-A`; no "Co-Authored-By" or "Generated with Claude Code" lines in commits; `events` is append-only; never bulk-delete prod `organization` rows; **workers never receive real credentials**; never introduce a new table or change DB/API/SDK surface without explicit user confirmation first; show the actual `git diff` rather than a prose summary before claiming done; run mandated gates automatically without asking; never `--admin` past a check that has not reported; end reports with a confidence score and 2–4 concrete next actions; prefer DOM reads over screenshots; never poll in the foreground.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **Drift gate three-way attribution**: `desired` (config) / `remote` (cloud) / `attribution` (effective remote after last succeeded apply). Converge when `remote == attribution`; block when `remote ≠ attribution AND desired ≠ remote`.
   - **`owned` set**: kind-qualified incarnation identities (`entity-type:12`, `watcher:b-1`, `connector-definition:5`) gating delete eligibility.
   - **`recorded` flag** (shipped in #2686): distinguishes "no baseline was ever recorded" from "a recorded baseline that happens to be empty."
   - **The no-baseline branch is the rollback + create path**, not a legacy shim (`rollback-cmd.ts:236` calls `computeDiff(state, remote, {})` deliberately).
   - **`bin/lobu.js` loads `../dist/index.js`** — editing `src` without `bun run build` runs the previous build. `dist/index.js` is a ~44KB entry shim; real modules are at `dist/commands/_lib/apply/*.js`.
   - **`make review-fix` writes after its first output flush** — acting on a `tail` instead of the completion notification cost a Depot attestation.
   - **Security boundary for value rendering**: the two-way `buildDiffRow` path covers secret-bearing always-update rows (provider keys, BYO connection `config`, auth profiles). Only three-way (baseline-aware) rows may carry `changedValues`.
   - `make pre-pr-remote` (full Linux CI on Depot against the *staged* tree, records a tree-hash attestation), `make review` (pi-review verdict), `make ui-review`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **MERGED — PR #2686, squash `9411ee0c5`** (11 files, +278/−97), worktree `apply-bootstrap-render`:
   - `packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/diff.ts` — added `recorded: boolean` as first field of `Baseline`; four `if (!baseline)` → `if (!baseline?.recorded)`; `remoteOnlyDefinitionRow` renamed param `legacyDelete` → `prune`.
   - `packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/deployment.ts` — `toBaseline(null)` now returns `recorded: false`.
   - `packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/apply-cmd.ts` — `recordableBaseline` for `--only agents` returns `baselineRecord ?? undefined` instead of synthesizing an empty record (the write-side half of the bug, found by `review-fix`).
   - Plus `client.ts`, `rollback-cmd.ts`, 5 test files, `docs/plans/lobu-apply-drift-gate.md`.

   **PR A (in flight) — worktree `/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/apply-prune-block`, branch `feat/apply-prune-block`, base `9411ee0c5`.** 3 files staged: `docs/plans/lobu-apply-drift-gate.md`, `packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/diff.ts`, `packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/__tests__/diff-baseline.test.ts`.

   `remoteOnlyDefinitionRow` final state:
   ```ts
   function remoteOnlyDefinitionRow(
     kind: "entity-type" | "relationship-type" | "watcher",
     remote: { slug: string; id?: number | string },
     baseline: Baseline | undefined,
     prune: boolean,
     unchangedSinceBaseline: (slug: string) => boolean
   ): DiffRow {
     // Off prune this apply cannot delete the definition, so blocking on it
     // protects nothing and only stalls the rest of the plan. Connector
     // definitions already scope their delete/block pair this way.
     if (!prune) {
       return { kind, verb: "drift", id: remote.slug, remote } as DiffRow;
     }
     // Prune may delete only a recorded, owned incarnation that is unchanged;
     // unowned, edited, and unrecorded all block, since deleting the wrong
     // definition is unrecoverable.
     const owned =
       baseline?.recorded === true &&
       remote.id !== undefined &&
       baseline.owned.has(ownedKey(kind, remote.id));
     if (owned && unchangedSinceBaseline(remote.slug)) {
       return { kind, verb: "delete", id: remote.slug, remote } as DiffRow;
     }
     return { kind, verb: "drift", blocking: true, id: remote.slug, remote } as DiffRow;
